The failure of an aircraft or engine manufacturer to meet its delivery obligations to us could negatively affect our cash flow
and results of operations.
The supply of commercial aircraft is dominated by Airbus and Boeing and a limited number of engine manufacturers. As
a result, we are dependent on these manufacturers remaining financially stable, producing aircraft which meet our lessees’
requirements and fulfilling contractual obligations they have to us.
